    {
      "title": "Kolkata pandal stampede LIVE | At least 19 dead, 25 others injured; CM Adhikari announces ₹25 lakh ex gratia",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/kolkata/kolkata-bengal-pandal-collapse-stampede-injured-death-updates-on-october-17-2026/article71597549.ece",
      "description": "Police detained 12 people, including organisers of the Chorebagan Durga Puja in connection with their probe into the stampede",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-10-18T01:10:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "Puja pandal stampede: PM announces ₹2 lakh ex gratia, Shah to visit injured",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/kolkata-puja-pandal-stampede-pm-announces-2-lakh-ex-gratia-amit-shah-to-visit-injured-126101701024_1.html",
      "description": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Saturday said the stampede in Kolkata is extremely distressing and announced an ex gratia of Rs 2 lakh to the next of kin of each deceased and Rs 50,000 for the injured.\nAt least 10 people are feared dead in a stampede following a crowd surge at a community Durga Puja pandal in north Kolkata on Saturday evening.\n\"The stampede in Kolkata is extremely distressing. My thoughts are with those who have lost their loved ones. May the injured recover at the earliest,\" Modi said in a post on X.\nThe prime minister said the local administration is providing all possible assistance to those affected.\nModi announced that an ex gratia of Rs 2 lakh will be given from the Prime Minister's National Relief Fund to the next of kin of each of those who lost their lives and Rs 50,000 to each injured person.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T17:54:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "At least 17 dead, 25 injured in stampede at Durga Puja pandal in Kolkata",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/at-least-25-injured-in-crowd-surge-at-durga-puja-pandal-in-north-kolkata-126101700952_1.html",
      "description": "At least 25 people were injured in a stampede-like situation arising out of a crowd surge at a community Durga Puja in north Kolkata on Saturday evening, police said.\nAs it started raining, the crowd waiting outside the Chorbagan Durga Puja pandal rushed forward, and some of them fell on the road, leading to the stampede-like situation, a senior officer said.\n\"At least 25 people were taken to the Kolkata Medical College and Hospital in serious condition,\" he said.\nWest Bengal Health Minister Saradwat Mukherjee and senior officials rushed to the hospital.\nDisaster management personnel rushed to the spot.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-17T16:38:17"
    }
  ]
